        "uid": "nvd:CVE-2026-119716",
        "tier": "1",
        "source_id": "nvd_critical",
        "source_name": "NVD \u2014 newly published CVEs, CVSS 9.0+",
        "title": "CVE-2026-119716 (CVSS 9.8)",
        "url": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-119716",
        "date": "2026-11-03",
        "summary": "pybars3 through 0.9.7 and pybars4 through 0.9.13 contain a code injection vulnerability in pybars/_compiler.py that allows template authors to execute Python code via unescaped bracketed path segments. Attackers can supply Handlebars templates with crafted segments in helper or block arguments to break out of string literals and execute Python in the application process.",
        "author": null
      },
      {
        "uid": "nvd:CVE-2026-102435",
        "tier": "1",
        "source_id": "nvd_critical",
        "source_name": "NVD \u2014 newly published CVEs, CVSS 9.0+",
        "title": "CVE-2026-102435 (CVSS 9.8)",
        "url": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-102435",
        "date": "2026-11-03",
        "summary": "The Ultra Addons for Contact Form 7 plugin for WordPress is vulnerable to arbitrary file deletion due to insufficient file path validation in the _getObjAttr function in all versions up to, and including, 3.5.54. This makes it possible for unauthenticated attackers to delete arbitrary files on the server, which can easily lead to remote code execution when the right file is deleted (such as wp-config.php). This requires the PDF Generator add-on to be active and a Contact Form 7 form to be configured for PDF generation, as the WPCF7_Submission POP gadget chain relies on CF7 being present to complete the file deletion via __destruct(). Note: This vulnerability can only be exploited when the PDF generator feature is enabled.",
        "author": null
      },
      {
        "uid": "nvd:CVE-2026-86596",
        "tier": "1",
        "source_id": "nvd_critical",
        "source_name": "NVD \u2014 newly published CVEs, CVSS 9.0+",
        "title": "CVE-2026-86596 (CVSS 9.8)",
        "url": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-86596",
        "date": "2026-11-03",
        "summary": "The s2Member plugin for WordPress is vulnerable to Remote Code Execution in all versions up to, and including, <= 260927 via the 'item_name' parameter parameter. This is due to insufficient sanitization in strip_php_tags_deep(), which only strips literal '<?' sequences, combined with a post-interpolation placeholder cleanup that reassembles a valid '<?php' opener after the attacker-controlled value has already been embedded in the email template. This makes it possible for authenticated attackers, with custom-level access and above, to execute code on the server.",
        "author": null
      },
      {
        "uid": "nvd:CVE-2026-120518",
        "tier": "1",
        "source_id": "nvd_critical",
        "source_name": "NVD \u2014 newly published CVEs, CVSS 9.0+",
        "title": "CVE-2026-120518 (CVSS 9.1)",
        "url": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-120518",
        "date": "2026-11-03",
        "summary": "The BuddyPress XProfile Image Field plugin for WordPress is vulnerable to arbitrary file deletion in all versions up to, and including, 3.1.0. This is due to bpxp_image_field_update_on_user_activation() calling unlink() on a path built from visitor-supplied signup metadata with no realpath() resolution, no containment check against the profile-image directory and no extension allow-list. Submitting a zero-byte file with the 'field_N_hidden' parameter during registration makes the plugin store the raw value, which is then resolved against the document root when the pending signup is activated. This makes it possible for unauthenticated attackers to delete arbitrary files on the server, which can easily lead to remote code execution when the right file (such as wp-config.php) is deleted. Requires open registration and an image-type profile field on the signup form.",
        "author": null
      },
      {
        "uid": "nvd:CVE-2026-120534",
        "tier": "1",
        "source_id": "nvd_critical",
        "source_name": "NVD \u2014 newly published CVEs, CVSS 9.0+",
        "title": "CVE-2026-120534 (CVSS 9.8)",
        "url": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-120534",
        "date": "2026-11-03",
        "summary": "The Advanced Custom Fields: Extended PRO plugin for WordPress is vulnerable to Limited Code Injection in all versions up to, and including, 0.9.2.6 via the render_field function. This is due to insufficient validation of form configuration parameters before merging into field settings and passing to call_user_func_array in the render_field method. This makes it possible for unauthenticated attackers to call arbitrary WordPress functions with controlled arguments. Method 1 requires the administrator to enable the non-default 'shortcode_preview' setting for the target form, while Method 2 requires the server environment to lack OpenSSL functions, causing ACF Pro's acf_decrypt to fall back to unverified base64 decoding.",
        "author": null
      },
      {
