        "uid": "ghsa:GHSA-f9j6-8p6x-r9j6",
        "tier": "1",
        "source_id": "github_advisories",
        "source_name": "GitHub Security Advisories",
        "title": "GHSA-f9j6-8p6x-r9j6 \u2014 SD JWT JS: Tampered disclosures silently dropped instead of rejected",
        "url": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-f9j6-8p6x-r9j6",
        "date": "2026-11-02",
        "summary": "## Summary\n\nWhen one Disclosure in an SD-JWT presentation is tampered so its digest no longer matches the Issuer-signed `_sd` array, `@sd-jwt/decode` 0.19.0 does **not** reject the presentation. It silently drops the unmatched Disclosure and returns a **reduced claim set**, reporting success. The Issuer signature is untouched and valid.\n\nThis is a downgrade/omission primitive. A malicious or curious **holder** can present a tampered Disclosure and have the relying party receive *fewer* claims than the credential carries, with no error surfaced. Where the relying party does **not** enforce key ",
        "author": null
      }
